      bullCase: "The increasing political engagement of crypto figures, as exemplified by Chris Larsen, signals the industry\'s growing maturity and ability to influence policy, which could lead to a more favorable regulatory environment for innovation. Furthermore, the rapid detection and public discourse around security breaches like the Ledger incident can drive accelerated improvements in industry-wide security standards and user education, ultimately strengthening the ecosystem\'s resilience.",
      bearCase: "The sophisticated supply chain attack on Ledger wallets and the autonomous crypto theft by an AI agent pose significant threats to user trust and the fundamental security narrative of the crypto market. These incidents could trigger a wave of regulatory backlash, leading to stricter controls on hardware manufacturers, AI development, and overall crypto operations, potentially stifling growth and deterring new investment.",
      neutralCase: "The current situation presents a mixed bag of challenges and opportunities. While security vulnerabilities are concerning, they are also catalysts for innovation in areas like supply chain verification and AI safety. The political involvement, though aggressive, could lead to more informed policy discussions. The market will likely experience short-term volatility due to FUD, but long-term adoption will hinge on the industry\'s ability to effectively address these multifaceted risks and build greater trust.",
